<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Expand <m>{\left(2x+5\right)^{3}}</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="30" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The powers of the first term go down, the powers of the second term go up, and every term has total power <m>{3}</m>. The coefficients for power <m>{3}</m> are 1, 3, 3, 1. Put <m>a = {2 x}</m> and <m>b = {5}</m> into each term, with brackets:</p><p><me>{\left(2x\right)^{3} + 3\left(2x\right)^{2}\left(5\right) + 3\left(2x\right)\left(5\right)^{2} + \left(5\right)^{3}}</me></p><p>Working out each term gives <m>{8 x^3+60 x^2+150 x+125}</m>.</p><p>Check: putting <m>x = 1</m> gives <m>({7})^{3} = {343}</m> on both sides.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>8 x^3+60 x^2+150 x+125</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>